{"title":"Reflection on the MSc Project","markdown":{"headingText":"Reflection on the MSc Project","containsRefs":false,"markdown":"\n### Project Summary\n\nMy MSc project evaluated the feasibility of using locally hosted Multimodal Large Language Models (MLLMs) to computationally integrate and analyse both qualitative and quantitative clinical trial data. Using a dataset from the LQD trial for treatment-resistant depression, I designed and applied three mixed-method analytical tasks: Convergence, Explanatory, and Statistical. Because a human expert baseline was unavailable, I developed an automated \"LLM-as-a-Judge\" evaluation strategy using custom scoring rubrics to assess the model's output. The project successfully demonstrated that MLLMs exhibit strong logical reasoning and factual consistency when triangulating clinical data, providing a foundational framework for future computational clinical analysis.\n\n### Skills Developed\n\nThroughout the research process, I developed advanced technical data analysis and project management skills, specifically by deploying and configuring language models on a High-Performance Cluster (CREATE). I also significantly enhanced my critical thinking and problem-solving abilities by designing multi-stage \"chain-of-thought\" prompting pipelines and systematically evaluating the complex logical relationships generated by the AI.\n\n### Challenges and Solutions\n\n|  |  |\n|----|----|\n| **Challenge** | **How I Overcame It** |\n| **Out-Of-Memory (OOM) Errors:** Limited computing resources on the HPC caused frequent memory crashes during analysis. | I implemented model quantization to load weights in 4-bit precision, utilized memory-efficient scaled dot-product attention, and divided massive qualitative transcripts into smaller, memory-safe batches. |\n| **Clinical Misinterpretation:** The model incorrectly assumed a lower QIDS-SR score indicated more severe depression symptoms. | I refined the prompt engineering by adding targeted system prompts that explicitly provided the correct clinical context and scale interpretation. |\n| **Data Pipeline Failures:** The LLM-generated Python code failed to locate specific data columns in the unseen quantitative dataset. | I updated the prompt instructions to include a detailed glossary of variable names, ensuring the model had the necessary context to generate functional code. |\n","srcMarkdownNoYaml":""},"formats":{"html":{"identifier":{"display-name":"HTML","target-format":"html","base-format":"html"},"execute":{"fig-width":7,"fig-height":5,"fig-format":"retina","fig-dpi":96,"df-print":"default","error":false,"eval":true,"cache":null,"freeze":false,"echo":true,"output":true,"warning":true,"include":true,"keep-md":false,"keep-ipynb":false,"ipynb":null,"enabled":null,"daemon":null,"daemon-restart":false,"debug":false,"ipynb-filters":[],"ipynb-shell-interactivity":null,"plotly-connected":true,"engine":"markdown"},"render":{"keep-tex":false,"keep-typ":false,"keep-source":false,"keep-hidden":false,"prefer-html":false,"output-divs":true,"output-ext":"html","fig-align":"default","fig-pos":null,"fig-env":null,"code-fold":"none","code-overflow":"scroll","code-link":false,"code-line-numbers":false,"code-tools":false,"tbl-colwidths":"auto","merge-includes":true,"inline-includes":false,"preserve-yaml":false,"latex-auto-mk":true,"latex-auto-install":true,"latex-clean":true,"latex-min-runs":1,"latex-max-runs":10,"latex-makeindex":"makeindex","latex-makeindex-opts":[],"latex-tlmgr-opts":[],"latex-input-paths":[],"latex-output-dir":null,"link-external-icon":false,"link-external-newwindow":false,"self-contained-math":false,"format-resources":[],"notebook-links":true},"pandoc":{"standalone":true,"wrap":"none","default-image-extension":"png","to":"html","output-file":"Chpt2_Project_Portfolio.html"},"language":{"toc-title-document":"Table of contents","toc-title-website":"On this page","related-formats-title":"Other Formats","related-notebooks-title":"Notebooks","sour